id: pm-jev-xgo9
title: Expand independent duplicate ground truth across public repositories
description: "The precision-first benchmark assigns whole repositories before inference, but available public duplicate closures leave only two held-out positive pairs. Add independently adjudicated duplicate and nonduplicate labels from additional public tracker repositories, record provenance and label disagreements, and freeze a new repository split before any model evaluation. Do not treat correlated closure-component siblings as independent evidence or retune the existing held-out set."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T15:00:08.751Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T15:06:26.792Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-jev-0w3q
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T15:06:06.126Z",codex-agent,"Discovered while implementing pm-jev-vouf: the fixed repository split yields only two held-out positives from the available public closure corpus. This follow-up owns independent public annotation and additional source repositories; it must use a fresh frozen split rather than tune the current held-out set."
